</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To create our answer set, given a generated query, we parse the infobox corresponding to each subject and query to extract the relevant information. We utilize the temporal markers mentioned in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2.5. TLQA from infoboxes ‣ 3.2. TLQA generation ‣ 3. Benchmark Creation ‣ Evaluating List Construction and Temporal Understanding capabilities of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to compile comprehensive answers. For sports-related queries, we extract the teams and the corresponding years the subject played for each team. For political-related queries, we extract the political positions held and the associated time periods. If the end year for a position or team association is not specified, we interpret this as an indication that the subject currently holds the position or remains with the team, aligning with the convention used on Wikipedia.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>. </span><span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dataset statistics along with categories.</span></figcaption>
